# PART B: Router-on-a-Stick – R2 and VLAN 40

## 8. Router Configuration – R2

Configure the R2 subinterface for VLAN 40.

```
enable
configure terminal

interface e0/0.40
 encapsulation dot1q 40
 ip address 192.168.40.1 255.255.255.0
 exit

interface e0/0
 no shutdown
 exit

end
write memory
```

The IP address `192.168.40.1` will act as the default gateway for devices in VLAN 40.

## 9. Switch Configuration – VLAN 40

### Step 1: Create VLAN 40

```
enable
configure terminal

vlan 40
 name London
 exit
```

### Step 2: Configure Trunk Port

Configure Ethernet 0/0 as the trunk link between the switch and R2.

```
interface e0/0
 switchport trunk encapsulation dot1q
 switchport mode trunk
 switchport trunk allowed vlan 40
 no shutdown
 exit
```

### Step 3: Configure Access Port

Configure Ethernet 0/1 as an access port for VLAN 40.

```
interface e0/1
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 40
 no shutdown
 exit

end
write memory
```

## 10. PC4 Configuration

Configure PC4 with an IP address in the VLAN 40 subnet.

```
ip 192.168.40.3/24 192.168.40.1
save
```

| Setting         | Value         |
| --------------- | ------------- |
| IP Address      | 192.168.40.3  |
| Subnet Mask     | 255.255.255.0 |
| Default Gateway | 192.168.40.1  |
| VLAN            | 40 – London   |

## 11. Verification – Network 2

### On the Switch

```
show vlan brief
show interfaces trunk
```

### On R2

```
show ip interface brief
show ip route
```

### From PC4

Test connectivity to the default gateway:

```
ping 192.168.40.1
```

Expected result: PC4 successfully reaches the R2 VLAN 40 gateway.

